    "scoring": {
      "_comment": "Internal scorer tie-break weights for substats PRESENT on the piece but NOT in the rule's selected substats (selected lines always score at their real weight). FIXED per-line bonuses — deliberately NOT scaled by roll value: the epsilon only marks a line's category; comparing roll quality is the real weights' job. Tier ladder, each far below weight.min (0.01) so stacking can never outweigh an explicit user weight, and each clearing the 1e-9 score-tie window: nonFlatEpsilonWeight (1e-4) — every unselected non-flat line (spd/cr/cdmg/res/acc/%stats); selectedAlignedFlatEpsilonWeight (1e-6) — a flat HP/ATK/DEF line whose percent twin IS a selected substat; mainAlignedFlatEpsilonWeight (1e-6) — a flat line whose percent twin is the piece's own main stat (additive with the previous when both apply, so a doubly-aligned flat wins). Unrelated flats earn exactly 0. The whole ladder is INERT on slots whose substat pool has no percent variants (per allowedSubsBySlot — today only the amulet): demoting flats against percent twins is meaningless where twins can't roll, so amulets rank purely by selected substats + main-stat bonus. The two flat tiers share one value on purpose (equally strong relevance signals). No glyph terms. Improvement-chance math stays epsilon-free on both sides of its comparisons (its quantization grids dwarf these terms).",
      "nonFlatEpsilonWeight": 0.0001,
      "selectedAlignedFlatEpsilonWeight": 0.000001,
      "mainAlignedFlatEpsilonWeight": 0.000001
    }
  },
