  "_comment_anomalousAccessories": "'Anomalous Accessories' (Champion Proving Grounds jewelry with mode-scoped damage substats). All eight substat ids are CONFIRMED against docs/orig/anomalous.hsf, an RSL Helper sellfile whose eight rules match a screenshot one-for-one: 11=PvE DMG+, 12=PvP DMG+, 13=Boss DMG+, 14=DNG DMG+, 15=PvE DMG-, 16=PvP DMG-, 17=Boss DMG-, 18=DNG DMG- (this confirmed 14/15/17/18, which had been inferred from mode-order contiguity against the account-d gear-DB fixture, artifacts 264537-264539). The same sample fixes the HSF wire format: rules are ORDINARY — one substat line, IsFlat false (percent-shaped, matching the DB fl=0 lines), Condition '>=', the other three slots ID -1 padding — and the only special rule is the VALUE SCALE, hsfValueScale: displayed 0.25% stores as 25 and 2.25% as 225, i.e. hundredths of a percent, where classic percent stats store the plain number (docs/orig/rules.hsf: 5 = 5%). The sample also proves 0.25 granularity is expressible, so targets quantize to hundredths rather than to a coarse roll grid. DB storage is unchanged (values scale by 2^32; the damage-taken family stores negative magnitudes and folds to magnitude at ingest). rollValueByRank is the CONFIRMED per-rank per-line value: 5-star = 1.25% and 6-star = 1.5% are observed, and the series steps by a uniform 0.25 per rank, so ranks 1-4 (0.25/0.5/0.75/1.0) extrapolate along it and bottom out exactly on minTargetValue. The game does not currently offer anomalous accessories below 5 stars, so the low ranks are forward-looking rather than load-bearing. The step is FIXED: an anomalous line is always its rank value times the number of lines, with no per-roll variance and no dependence on the substat target the user set - which is why the 6-star value doubles as the normalization denominator (see SUBSTAT_ROLL_MAX_6_BY_VARIANT / safeguard_substat_max6_by_variant) and why the damage-taken family, folded to magnitude at ingest, normalizes identically to the dealt family. A rank-5 Banner with a set was observed, confirming Banner eligibility. Labels mirror the announcement wording; final in-game strings may differ. eligibleSets is announced and final (keys reference the artifactSet catalog above). These substats deliberately stay OUT of allowedSubsBySlot: that table feeds the Rust engine's substat-gap anticipation (see anomalousAccessories.ts). Full ledger: docs/technical/anomalous-accessories.md.",
